{
  "name": "regex-group-names-script-values",
  "description": "Group names and script values follow Dart's RegExp (ECMAScript), and a pattern Dart refuses makes the `regex` transform resolve to null (the client catches the error). The transform reads groups by number, so names ICU and the JVM refuse still work: `(?<$a>x)` with `g` and `(?<\u00e9>x)` with `gu` on \"x\" give \"#\", and one name in two alternatives with its reference, `(?:(?<a>x)|(?<a>y))\\k<a>` on \"xx yy xy\", gives \"# # xy\" (the reference matches the group that took part). Dart refuses a name twice in one alternative (`(?<a>x)(?<a>y)`) and a reference to a name no group has (`(?<a>x)\\k<b>`): null. A back reference that can only see its group unset matches empty: before its group closes (`(a\\1)` on \"aa\" gives \"##\"), in another alternative (`(a)|\\1b` on \"ab b\" gives \"## #\") and after a negative lookahead that holds the group (`(?!(a))\\1b` on \"b ab aa ba bb abb aab xy y x\" gives \"# a# aa #a ## a## aa# xy y x\"). With `gu` a script value must be a name in ECMAScript's table, matched exactly: Unicode's long names and four-letter codes, less Katakana_Or_Hiragana and Hrkt, plus the aliases Qaai (Inherited) and Qaac (Coptic). So `\\p{Script=latin}` (case), `\\p{Script=Hrkt}` and `\\p{Script=OldItalic}` (not in the table) and `\\p{Script=}` resolve to null. On \"a\", U+03B1 (Greek), U+0300 (Inherited), U+2C81 (Coptic), U+309B (Common) and U+0951 (Inherited), `\\p{Script=Latn}` replaces the \"a\"; `\\p{Script=Old_Italic}`, `\\p{Script=Zzzz}` and `\\p{Script=Unknown}` match nothing; `\\p{Script=Qaai}` (Inherited) replaces U+0300 and U+0951; and `\\p{Script=Qaac}` (Coptic) replaces U+2C81. Every replace-mode regex puts \"#\" for each match. Every input reads page state, so the engine keeps the Values unresolved with `watches` and the client resolves them.",
